<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Implementation details about the baselines are in the supplementary.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HM2F-Video:</span> The image encoder is the pre-trained Hiera-B+ from SAM 2 and the decoder architecture is adopted from Mask2Former-Video. During training, two consecutive frames were processed setting the batch size to <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>. We trained the model for <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32,\!000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32,\!000</annotation></semantics></math> iterations while keeping the learning rate equal to <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e\!-\!4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e\!-\!4</annotation></semantics></math>. The number of mask-decoder layers was set to <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math>, while the number of output queries is equal to <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CC-SAM2:</span> In CC-SAM2, we utilized SAM 2 with Hiera-B+ as image encoder. The model was trained for 40 epochs with a batch size of <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. The base learning rate is set to <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e\!-\!4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e\!-\!4</annotation></semantics></math>, and the input image resolution is 1024<math id="S5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>1024 pixels. The number of consecutive input video frames is set to <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Quantitative results on <span id="S5.T3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SOS</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>. We compare our proposed baselines, CC-SAM2 and HM2F-Video, to various state-of-the-art methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>. Best results are in <span id="S5.T3.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span> and second best are <span id="S5.T3.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span>.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S5.T3.8" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:341.6pt;height:94.3pt;vertical-align:-45.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-181.3pt,50.1pt) scale(0.485082947567484,0.485082947567484) ;">
