<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S5.F4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative Results<span id="S5.F4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. Road-obstacle prediction maps from RbA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>, Mask2Anomaly <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>, HM2F-Video and CC-SAM2 on the SOS dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>. HM2F-Video accurately segments road-obstacles across temporal frames.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="S5.T5.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Quantitative results on Apolloscape-Road-Obstacle. Best results are in <span id="S5.T5.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span> and second best are <span id="S5.T5.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span>. <math id="S5.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\dagger}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\dagger}}</annotation></semantics></math> are video-based road obstacle segmentation methods.</span></figcaption>
